<Defs>

  <!--
    The crops the colony can grow, one Def per species.

    ORDER IS NOT DECIDED HERE. A zone record stores its plant as a handle, and
    WorldContent.PlantOrder is the list that decides which name is which handle, exactly as
    TerrainOrder does for terrain. The order below is the same one only so the file reads as
    the table does.

    The numbers are docs/design/22-growing.md §2. growTicks counts growing-window ticks, not
    clock ticks: 130,000 window ticks is four 60,000-tick days at the 32,500-tick daylight
    window, with a quarter of the bar filling on day one so progress is visible. sowWorkTicks
    includes breaking the cell's grass; the terrain itself is never changed by a sowing.
    minFertility is per cent against ordinary soil — 70 admits grass (100) and bare earth
    (85) and refuses gravel (55), because carrots in gravel read as a bug.
  -->

  <PlantDef>
    <defName>Plant_Carrot</defName>
    <label>carrot</label>
    <description>A root vegetable that keeps without fuss and eats raw. Sows by hand into
    open soil and stands three seasons of a day each before the cut.</description>
    <growTicks>130000</growTicks>
    <sowWorkTicks>170</sowWorkTicks>
    <harvestWorkTicks>200</harvestWorkTicks>
    <yieldCount>5</yieldCount>
    <yields>Item_Carrots</yields>
    <minFertility>70</minFertility>
  </PlantDef>

</Defs>
